<title>UK: UK Parliament to hold extended debate on EMU.</title>
<headline>UK Parliament to hold extended debate on EMU.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-11-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>The British government has agreed to hold an &quot;extended&quot; debate on European Economic and Monetary Union in Parliament ahead of next month's EU summit in Dublin, an aide to Prime Minister John Major said on Monday.</p>
<p>He was speaking after what he described as a &quot;constructive&quot; 25-minute meeting between Major and senior officials of the 1922 Committee, the grouping of Conservative Members of Parliament who are not ministers.</p>
<p>The aide said the exact length and duration of the debate, which will be on an anodyne motion for the adjournment of the House of Commons, has yet to be decided.</p>
</text>
